  "checks": [
    "For 0<t<d<L, min(t,L-t)>=t*(L-d)/L. The raw radicand lower and the true factorization F=t*g imply g>=kappa*(L-d)/L; continuity extends this to the whole closed half including the root.",
    "Both orientations use the same inwardComponentPoint convention and the actual optical cut. The reciprocal cost is total component length times kappa inverse times the opposite physical half width inverse.",
    "The already-proved return-margin host provides both half widths. A fixed radial coefficient power is absorbed at that real host sample and transferred by the new90 source to the original sample attached to any selected half. Host cells are never identified.",
    "The same global smooth division from the existing154 provider is selected before any derivative order. Its jets on the entire closed component retain their existing one-derivative division cost and transfer to the original half sample.",
    "The reciprocal kappa cost is exactly K0*E0(hostsample)^K0; it is transported to the same half sample and multiplied by the opposite-half cost. Exponents add only using actual positivity of E0.",
    "All common constants and all-order coefficient sequences precede component, host, side and point. Original E0 is not assumed to be at least one; no local root-model radius or extension derivative enters the numerical cost."
  ],
